{"title":"Mock AIME 1 2010 Problems/Problem 9","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_2010_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/d/cddbccf89c00e019e9878f87f8d6325697e3f2fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/e/7cef5fa7ec053472a6e471aaacb0c5927ce36b36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> be circles of radii 5 and 7, respectively, and suppose that the distance between their centers is 10. There exists a circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/d/05d0bb1172cf128548aec51cabd885258e296e6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" /> that is internally tangent to both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/d/cddbccf89c00e019e9878f87f8d6325697e3f2fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/e/7cef5fa7ec053472a6e471aaacb0c5927ce36b36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" />, and tangent to the line joining the centers of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/d/cddbccf89c00e019e9878f87f8d6325697e3f2fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/e/7cef5fa7ec053472a6e471aaacb0c5927ce36b36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" />. If the radius of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/d/05d0bb1172cf128548aec51cabd885258e296e6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" /> can be expressed in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/2/152a93116566a3c996445d054b59186bccd6f353.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\sqrt{b} - c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"63\" height=\"18\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> are integers, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> is not divisible by the square if any prime, find the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/d/2cdfeae33c1e09de6207d446beb72396c04be481.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + b + c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"72\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_2010_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/e/6fea45481c9ba0dad5c9d8017acea99064148436.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]  import geometry;  size(10cm);  point A = origin; point B = (10,0); point C = (5-(30-2*sqrt(210)),10*sqrt(210)-144); point D,E,T;  circle a = circle(A,5); circle b = circle(B,7); circle c = circle(C,10*sqrt(210)-144);  // Defining D, E, and T pair[] d = intersectionpoints(b,A--B); D = d[0];  pair[] e = intersectionpoints(a,A--B); E = e[0];  pair[] t = intersectionpoints(c,A--B); T = t[0];  // Circles draw(a); draw(b); draw(c);  // Segments AB, BC, AC, and CT draw(A--B); draw(B--C); draw(A--C); draw(C--T);  // Point Labels dot(A); label(&quot;A&quot;,A,WSW); dot(B); label(&quot;B&quot;,B,ESE); dot(C); label(&quot;C&quot;,C,(0,0.5)); dot(D); label(&quot;D&quot;,D,SW); dot(E); label(&quot;E&quot;,E,SE); dot(T); label(&quot;T&quot;,T,S);  // Right angle mark markscalefactor=0.05; draw(rightanglemark(C,T,A));  [/asy]\" width=\"475\" height=\"302\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/d/cddbccf89c00e019e9878f87f8d6325697e3f2fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> have center <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/e/7cef5fa7ec053472a6e471aaacb0c5927ce36b36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> have center <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/d/05d0bb1172cf128548aec51cabd885258e296e6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" /> have center <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Further, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> intersect <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/d/cddbccf89c00e019e9878f87f8d6325697e3f2fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/e/7cef5fa7ec053472a6e471aaacb0c5927ce36b36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/d/05d0bb1172cf128548aec51cabd885258e296e6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, as in the diagram. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be the radius of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/d/05d0bb1172cf128548aec51cabd885258e296e6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" /> and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/f/eaf2ba84ded0b3edeb5886ac07a8b17e7a32ad14.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$TE=x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> is tangent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/d/05d0bb1172cf128548aec51cabd885258e296e6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/b/85bf4411deb98e913f1a12b146e7ae44422b0aec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{CT} \\perp \\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"82\" height=\"18\" />. Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/d/cddbccf89c00e019e9878f87f8d6325697e3f2fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/d/05d0bb1172cf128548aec51cabd885258e296e6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" /> are tangent, we know that the line joining their centers goes through their point of tangency. Thus, because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/d/cddbccf89c00e019e9878f87f8d6325697e3f2fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> has radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/0/ac0be08f46215b70055262b838c7347a1a9e08e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC=5-r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"16\" />. Similarly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/0/a3029227cdcdf25b1755183b9e1ca8eee1c7c2ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC=7-r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"95\" height=\"16\" />. Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/4/6c4b41dd37dcc418b2bd81d72c4d763936a2fc76.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=10$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/8/5c884057c1218625814fc38808eb0f395aac6928.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE=5$\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/a/07a80c2f2fadf847e91ca9ec97eb22ccdf643655.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD=7$\" width=\"63\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/2/d5204a6910d20a4ff2968ad55671e3cfa350e9da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=2$\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/2/9c262fa32802dc907025f6ecd39770656b3f6821.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DT=2-x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"96\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/e/b3ed4de2791bca06e909e8dab5b3e35862934e72.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD=5-2=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"129\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/f/9efa1f32bb12f5472d811e87a6008580620d5d2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BE=7-2=5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"129\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>By the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pythagorean_Theorem\" title=\"Pythagorean Theorem\">Pythagorean Theorem</a> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/1/0f15fd3d4b6b84f274c198ebbc221662108dbf6d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BTC$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" />, we have the following equation that we can solve for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />:\n\\begin{align*}\nBT^2+TC^2 &amp;= BC^2 \\\\\n(5+x)^2+r^2 &amp;= (7-r)^2 \\\\\n25+10x+x^2+r^2 &amp;= 49-14r+r^2 \\\\\nx^2+10x-24 &amp;= -14r \\\\\nr &amp;= -\\frac{x^2+10x-24}{14}\n\\end{align*}\nBy using Pythagoras again in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/c/aac3610fd781fd50cf208bcd2e87a92dceb110f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ATC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"59\" height=\"18\" />, we have the following equation:\n\\begin{align*}\nAT^2+TC^2 &amp;= AC^2 \\\\\n(3+(2-x))^2+r^2 &amp;= (5-r)^2 \\\\\n(5-x)^2+r^2 &amp;= r^2-10r+25 \\\\\nx^2-10x+25 &amp;= -10r+25 \\\\\nx^2-10x &amp;= -10r\n\\end{align*}\nSubstituting the expression for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> we found earlier, we see the following:\n\\begin{align*}\nx^2-10x &amp;= -10(-\\frac{x^2+10x-24}{14}) \\\\\nx^2-10x &amp;= \\frac{5x^2+50x-120}{7} \\\\\n7x^2-70x &amp;= 5x^2+50x-120 \\\\\n2x^2-120x+120 &amp;= 0 \\\\\nx^2-60x+60 &amp;= 0 \\\\\nx &amp;= \\frac{60 \\pm \\sqrt{3600-240}}2 \\\\\nx &amp;= 30 \\pm \\sqrt{900-60} \\\\\nx &amp;= 30 \\pm 2\\sqrt{210}\n\\end{align*}\nBecause <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/2/3123986e9c31a9b7f740325866cfdeb186219ad7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&lt;2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/e/4ae5e6231638fec0d4e609385cadca210366954f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=30 - 2\\sqrt{210}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"128\" height=\"21\" />. Now, we can plug this value for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> into our expression for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> to get our answer:\n\\begin{align*}\nr &amp;= -\\frac{x^2+10x-24}{14} \\\\\n&amp;= -\\frac{(30-2\\sqrt{210})^2+10(30-2\\sqrt{210})-24}{14} \\\\\n&amp;= -\\frac{900+840-120\\sqrt{210}+300-20\\sqrt{210}-24}{14} \\\\\n&amp;= -\\frac{1740+276-140\\sqrt{210}}{14} \\\\\n&amp;= 10\\sqrt{210}-\\frac{2016}{14} \\\\\n&amp;= 10\\sqrt{210}-144\n\\end{align*}\nThus, our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/d/50d3ea095aff262937b0bdfd145004452f1256ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10+210+144=\\boxed{364}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"182\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_2010_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_2010\" title=\"Mock AIME 1 2010\">Mock AIME 1 2010</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_2010_Problems\" title=\"Mock AIME 1 2010 Problems\">Problems</a></b>, <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/viewtopic.php?t={{{source}}}\">Source</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_2010_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"Mock AIME 1 2010 Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_2010_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"Mock AIME 1 2010 Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_2010_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"Mock AIME 1 2010 Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_2010_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"Mock AIME 1 2010 Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_2010_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"Mock AIME 1 2010 Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_2010_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"Mock AIME 1 2010 Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_2010_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"Mock AIME 1 2010 Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_2010_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"Mock AIME 1 2010 Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_2010_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"Mock AIME 1 2010 Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_2010_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"Mock AIME 1 2010 Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_2010_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"Mock AIME 1 2010 Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_2010_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Mock AIME 1 2010 Problems/Problem 11 (page does not exist)\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_2010_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Mock AIME 1 2010 Problems/Problem 12 (page does not exist)\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_2010_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"Mock AIME 1 2010 Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_2010_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Mock AIME 1 2010 Problems/Problem 14 (page does not exist)\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_2010_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Mock AIME 1 2010 Problems/Problem 15 (page does not exist)\">15</a>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018035746\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.031 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.062 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 349/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1355/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 101/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 10594/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.409      1 Template:Mock_AIME_box\n100.00%    7.409      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:28406:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018035746 and revision id 224250. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}